client.tools(defs, { callToolTimeoutMs }) passes a per-call request timeout
to the MCP SDK for plain and task-based tool calls, so a long-running tool
is not cut off at the SDK's 60-second default. Upstream has no equivalent
option in 0.4.6. Remove when an @tanstack/ai-mcp release offers one.

